      "created_at": "2022-01-28T21:22:17Z",
      "updated_at": "2022-01-28T21:22:17Z",
      "body": "It is up for us who write software to decide what the software does, and it is up to you to decide if you want to use it. E-mail is the centerpiece of authentication in Mastodon from day 1 and requiring e-mail confirmation is an important feature that benefits the fediverse, as any server that does not require it would become a vector for spam for everyone else in the network (see the 10minutepleroma incident). So yes, it sounds like Mastodon is not for you.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
